CORE
backward_goto_fallthrough.c
--unwind 3 --unwinding-assertions --paths lifo
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With --paths, resuming the saved jump-target path of the backward goto
"goto back" continues at the instruction after that goto, which is the head of
the inner loop. This transition is a forward one and must reset the inner
loop's unwinding counter, as it does without --paths.
